{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/160445-the-interlocks","id":160445,"title":"The Interlocks.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-05T18:50:25-07:00","id":160445,"title":"The Interlocks.","content":"I need your help forum-mates. I really do. I'm coming upon the third session of the Demon game I'm running and I just can't figure out a players Interlocks. I finished my other three player's in a night, but this character eludes me.<br /> <br /> She is a Messenger Inquisitor, hacktavist created to spread misinformation and cause havoc through use of the internet. (Basically relying people up so they take rage quitting to the extreme). She fell when she followed the threads of her lies and released just what kind of damage she was doing (Her last message was supposed to cause another Waco incident).<br /> The Embed she has chosen is Voice of the machine. Her preferred means of getting things accomplished are hacking (really likes to do or attempt it even if the situation doesn't call for it), she employs Parkour, silent moving (her specialty in stealth), and uses fear as a means of intimidation when needed. And I'm stumped. Just completely outta my head with what to do with her. Any help would be greatly appreciated. <br /> Or maybe just a bouncing board, I wanted to give her something that let her hook up with machine buts didn't want to negate her already existing hacking specialty. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T19:21:26-07:00","id":160474,"title":"","content":"Interlocks are a lot of work. I find it rewarding work, but I can't deny it takes a lot of effort out of you.<br /> <br /> As it happens, I'm actually playing a hacktivist demon myself, although the two characters sound like dark mirrors of one another. Could you share more about the character's personality and motives? Does she have an idea of what her vision of Hell and purpose for her Descent is, or is she still working that out? What ties her to the world and sparked her Fall, principles, philosophies, group identifications, individual friends or loved ones? Does she feel strongly about certain things or does she struggle with human emotion? Is she mischievous, thoughtful, circumspect, detached, cowardly, daring, deceitful, friendly, charismatic? Is her Cover identity a precious touchstone in the world or a convenient shroud that masks her true motives and nature? As well, what does the <i>player</i> enjoy about the game? Does she like involved mechanics or quick fixes, flashy stuff or deep thoughts? Does she prefer to keep her character out of the fray or is tagging along with the rest of the ring important?<br /> <br /> Any information of this sort will help; these are all just examples of the kinds of things that might suss out a direction to go with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T19:24:29-07:00","id":160477,"title":"","content":"As a general trend I've found that my characters' second Interlocks tend to be the ones most &quot;iconic&quot; to their skillsets, though I admittedly have a bad habit of working the things closer together than published examples indicate is the norm and it's more of a trend than a consistent occurrence. Got any ideas for her final secret or Keys?<br /> <br /> How would an Interlock that allows one to apply the principles of hacking in a broader scope via exploiting sympathy with the Machine sound?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T19:56:01-07:00","id":160491,"title":"","content":"the character is still working most of her inner most aspects out. She fell because she realized a professor she was becoming enamored with would have died in a siege between the City Police and what's basically a cult. She's a tag along with another Demon, a Tempter by the Name of Mr. Price. She's very content exploiting younger males if it means she can a job completed. As for what she enjoys. She really enjoys hacking, to the point where its become a joke to the other players &quot;We found a Ledger! Ms. Dot, try to hack it!&quot;<br /> <br /> Satchel, that's actually a really good idea. How could I develop that from &quot;Voice of the Machine?&quot;<br /> <br /> Currently this is my prototype for her cipher and final truth. <br /> Cipher: No Prophesies<br /> Final Truth: Chance and Luck are predetermined; nothing more than a series of events. Control the events now, to own the outcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T20:14:55-07:00","id":160500,"title":"","content":"There's a number of ways it could go, depending on which direction one took &quot;hacking with a broader scope&quot; in and what Key was used to get there; Right Tools, Right Job could be used to effectively quick-write a mundane object into a Gadget, for example, or Special Message could be leveraged to turn Voice of the Machine's principles toward decryption. It's important to remember that the effects of the Key Embeds are more of a jumping-off point than a strict merger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T20:35:53-07:00","id":160509,"title":"","content":"Voice of the Machine <b>&gt;</b> Social Dynamics<br /> <i>God emerges from the gap between its components.</i><br /> <b>Aether Map:</b> The demon can perceive the exhaust and reverberation of Aether. This enhanced Aether sense, given time to concentrate, can be used to form a sort of echolocation map of Infrastructure and other demonic and God-Machine related activity, and derive information about its nature and functioning.<br /> <br /> Social Dynamics <b>&gt;</b> Like I Built It<br /> <i>Emergent behavior alters the gestalt; know the pieces and you know the workings of the whole.</i><br /> <b>Crowdhack:</b> The demon understands how to use the personalities and relationships of people like variables and operations in a vast algorithm. She can plan out how to use minor social interactions with particular members spread out through a social group or organization to guide the actions and outlook of the whole.<br /> <br /> Like I Built It <b>&gt;</b> Mercury Retrograde<br /> <i>What we assume to be unitary systems are themselves vulnerable to the same method.</i><br /> <b>Soul Programming:</b> Through intense, intimate extended conversation with a character, the demon is able to mutate the character's Aspirations, Virtue or Vice into modified forms relating to their previous state. Reinforcement over long periods of time can shift the character's natural resting point for these traits, making drastic changes possible through persistent application across several transitive states.<br /> <br /> <b>ALL THINGS ARE BORN FROM INFORMATION.</b><br /> <i>Everything emerges from the tiniest interactions. Truth, beauty and the soul are malleable: to edit their input values is to craft them as you see fit.</i><br /> <br /> Control the input, and you become master of the output.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T21:13:25-07:00","id":160544,"title":"","content":"Very good points Satchel. Those are great Stupid Loserman, they actually fit really well with another player. I may have to swap out what I've already written for him. Thank's guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T10:28:06-07:00","id":160933,"title":"","content":"This is hopefully related but each time I read a Final Truth, it's a vague statement or set of statements. How does this help the player? I understand how it could help the Demon as it's a revelation, but how do I make it relevant to the player?<br /> <br /> Maybe this answers my own question but the only thing I can think of is design the Chronicle with each Final Truth in mind and gear the story to reward demons who follow their Cipher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T19:42:53-07:00","id":161350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/160445-the-interlocks?p=160509#post160509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>ALL THINGS ARE BORN FROM INFORMATION.</b><br /> <i>Everything emerges from the tiniest interactions. Truth, beauty and the soul are malleable: to edit their input values is to craft them as you see fit.</i><br /> <br /> Control the input, and you become master of the output.</div> </div> </div> </div>- Chairman Sheng-ji Yang, Essays on Mind and Matter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T06:02:54-07:00","id":161598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/160445-the-interlocks?p=161350#post161350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - Chairman Sheng-ji Yang, Essays on Mind and Matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trufax. I was refreshing myself on Alpha Centauri quotes for idea fodder when I wrote that Cipher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T21:38:19-07:00","id":162194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/160445-the-interlocks?p=160477#post160477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got any ideas for her final secret or Keys?<br /> <br /> How would an Interlock that allows one to apply the principles of hacking in a broader scope via exploiting sympathy with the Machine sound?</div> </div> </div> </div>Every time the player tries to add an embed to the cypher, make her say <i>why</i> she thinks that the next key... and take notes, and then use that information to determine what the player is looking for.<br /> <br /> For the Final Secret, read the <a href=\"http://www.phrack.org/archives/issues/7/3.txt\" target=\"_blank\">Hacker Manifesto</a>. Get an idea of the hacker mindset, the last two paragraphs especially look like the sort of Gnostic Truth a hacktivist demon might come to during their descent.<br /> <br /> The final interlock<br /> YOU CAN BREAK THE INDIVIDUAL: The Demon activates this Interlock when capture, destruction, or reintegration into the God Machine is inevitable. The Demon loses all knowledge or her Embeds, Exploits and Interlocks. These bits of data travel across the world and lodge themselves in the minds and souls of demons, stigmatics, and normal humans who are sympathetic to the Demon's personal vision of hell and have a willingness to strike against the God Machine. This includes the Interlock YOU CAN BREAK THE INDIVIDUAL which will install itself on whatever other demon the character the original user trusts the most. No beneficiary of this interlock may receive more than one embed or exploit per use of YOU CAN BREAK THE INDIVIDUAL.<br /> <br /> Concept: This more of a plot device than a usable power but it unites the ideals of hacktivism with those of the Descent : liberation/dissemination of information, a mass movement working to overthrow of a corrupt social order, and the demon leaves an immortal legacy that the God Machine cannot stamp out: becoming a reverse virus that empowers more and more individuals against the God Machine.<br /> <br /> From a game play standpoint, a character could explain the interlock as leverage against the angels, like a deadman switch (&quot;Kill me or integrate me, you're just making more trouble for yourself&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}